10. What Is Kafka Connect?

Kafka Connect is a framework for integrating Kafka with external systems.

It reduces the need to write custom producer and consumer applications for every integration.

It uses two main types of connectors.

Source connector

Moves data from an external system into Kafka.

Examples:

Database changes into Kafka.

Files or application data into Kafka.

Records from a supported external source into Kafka.


Sink connector

Moves data from Kafka to an external destination.

Examples:

Kafka events into object storage.

Kafka records into a supported database.

Kafka events into an analytical platform.


Architecture

Source Database
       |
       v
Source Connector
       |
       v
      Kafka
       |
       v
 Sink Connector
       |
       v
 Data Lake / Database

Interview answer:

> Kafka Connect is a framework used to integrate Kafka with external systems. Source connectors bring data into Kafka, while sink connectors send data from Kafka to destinations such as databases or data storage platforms. It supports reusable integrations without requiring custom ingestion code for every connection.




