15. Kafka Commands You Should Recognize

You do not need to memorize every command, but you should recognize common Kafka operations.

The following are illustrative commands for a Kafka environment where the corresponding command-line tools are installed and the cluster is configured appropriately.

List topics

kafka-topics.sh \
  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \
  --list

Lists available topics.

Create a topic

kafka-topics.sh \
  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \
  --create \
  --topic orders \
  --partitions 3 \
  --replication-factor 1

Creates a topic called orders with three partitions and a replication factor of one.

This replication factor is suitable only for environments that support it, such as a simple local development cluster. Production clusters typically use replication across multiple brokers.

Describe a topic

kafka-topics.sh \
  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \
  --describe \
  --topic orders

Displays topic configuration and partition information.

Produce messages

kafka-console-producer.sh \
  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \
  --topic orders

You can then type messages into the console producer.

Consume messages

kafka-console-consumer.sh \
  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \
  --topic orders \
  --from-beginning

Reads available retained records from the beginning of the topic.

The actual command names and installation paths may vary by Kafka distribution and version.

For an interview, focus on understanding what these commands do rather than claiming you have executed them if you haven't.


