20. Final Revision Sheet: The 10 Concepts You Must Know

Before a data engineering interview, make sure you can explain these concepts without reading your notes.

No.	Concept	What to remember

1	Kafka	Distributed event streaming platform
2	Producer	Publishes events
3	Consumer	Reads and processes events
4	Topic	Named stream of records
5	Partition	Ordered sequence of records that enables parallelism
6	Offset	Position of a record within a partition
7	Consumer group	Allows consumers to share partition processing
8	Broker	Kafka server that stores and serves records
9	Replication	Helps provide fault tolerance
10	Retention	Determines how long records remain available


Once you understand these, focus on the next five concepts:

1. Kafka vs. Spark.


2. Kafka Connect and CDC.


3. Consumer lag and rebalancing.


4. At-least-once vs. exactly-once processing.


5. Schema evolution and idempotency.




